  "note": "Held-out interventions and initialization-seed sensitivity on the corrected raw/X + unique_fragment_overlap inputs. The initialization-sensitivity claim now uses the declared pooled-donor estimand (same as the primary contrast): donor predictions are pooled across each repeat's held-out folds, each repeat's cross-attention minus token-concat donor balanced accuracy is averaged across repeats, and donors are resampled for the interval. Seed 0 reproduces the primary corrected estimate +0.0066667 and interval [-0.025, +0.0350074] exactly. Donor-level predictions are stored in the source run's donor_predictions.json. The intervention table now also aggregates each manipulation's direct numerical check (cell_flip_rate_mean and mean_confidence_drop_mean): within-donor permutation flips roughly 12-31% of held-out cell labels even though the donor-level metric drop is ~0, so the near-zero effect is not a no-op or floating-point artefact. Model dependence under a stated manipulation, not causal biology.",
